eli_s: Heads up — customer ACME (ticket ACME-471) is blocked. They call our OpenAI-compatible endpoint and the function/tool call fails schema validation in our backend. Logs show enum mismatch + args coming back as a JSON string. Repro and snippets below, needs eng triage.

maria: can you paste the raw request/response you see?

eli_s: sure — minimal repro they provided (sanitized):

```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/chat/completions 
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-REDACTED' 
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' 
  -d '{
    "model": "oa-compatible-1",
    "messages": [{"role":"user","content":"create widget"}],
    "functions": [{"name":"widget_create","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["CREATE","UPDATE"]}}}}],
    "function_call": "auto"
  }'
```

Response body in logs (exact):

```json
{
  "id":"resp-xyz",
  "choices":[{
    "message":{
      "role":"tool",
      "name":"widget_create",
      "content": null,
      "function_call":{
        "name":"widget_create",
        "arguments":"{\"id\":123, \"kind\": \"create\"}"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

eli_s: our validation layer expects `arguments` to be an object and `kind` enum values to be uppercase (CREATE/UPDATE). The result: parser rejects the call with "enum mismatch" and we return 400 to the customer.

sam_g: aha. Two things here: (1) "arguments" as a string is a known divergence from some model outputs — OpenAI can return stringified JSON. (2) enum casing differences are common across model families. We should normalize both in the compatibility normalizer.

maria: agree. Is this specific to oa-compatible-1 or seen across models?

sam_g: customer reported with that model, but we've seen similar from a third-party open model where enums are lowercase. I'll prepare a small compat patch that: try JSON.parse if arguments is string; coerce enum strings to canonical uppercase before schema check; and add logging when we coerce.

chris_pm: customer is on Dedicated with SLA, they're currently blocked. Mark P1 and involve oncall.

oncall-bot: @eng-oncall paging — support P1: ACME-471 function-call schema failures (enum casing + args string).

deploy-bot: CI pipeline kicked for branch fix/compat/parse-string-args (build #b1224).

sam_g: quick patch idea (node):

```js
function normalizeFunctionCall(fc){
  // fc.arguments may be a string or an object
  let args = fc.arguments;
  if(typeof args === 'string'){
    try{ args = JSON.parse(args); }catch(e){
      // fallback: attempt simple replace of single quotes or log and rethrow
      logger.info('compat: arguments JSON parse failed, returning original string');
    }
  }
  // normalize enums to uppercase if present
  if(args && typeof args.kind === 'string'){
    args.kind = args.kind.toUpperCase();
  }
  fc.arguments = args;
  return fc;
}
```

sam_g: will push canary to staging, run the unit that validates function_call -> schema mapping, and if green roll to canary in prod.

maria: add a regression test: model returns lowercase enum + stringified args -> our ingest should accept and produce same semantic tool call as if canonical.

eli_s: customer updated: "we can sit tight for canary, but need ETA" — please keep them in the loop.

sam_g: ETA ~30-45m for canary deploy. I'll post link to logs and tag the ticket.

oncall-bot: oncall acknowledged.

deploy-bot: canary started for fix/compat/parse-string-args -> prod-canary (2026-03-17T15:10:20Z).

sam_g: monitoring traces for ACME-471 now, will confirm when a successful function_call makes it through.

maria: also file a small doc note in eng-ml about models that stringify arguments and enum-casing quirks so we don't regress.

eli_s: thanks — looping chris_pm for customer comms.

chris_pm: I will email ACME with ETA and note we're rolling a fix to handle lowercase enums and string args; will ask them to retry after canary.

eli_s: :thumbsup:

sam_g: can confirm — first successful call seen in canary logs: function_call.arguments parsed and kind normalized to "CREATE". Pushing full rollout pending 10m observation.

eli_s: marking this thread resolved once full rollout completes and customer confirms.
